# Simulator-only parameters for the sd_fpv7 model (the 7-inch from hardware/cad/fpv7:
# X frame, 2807 1300KV, 7x4 three-blade propellers, 6S2P 10 000 mAh). Loaded after the
# safety parameters. Only SIM_*, the names in tools/params_allowlist.toml and, for this
# model, its [vehicles.sd_fpv7] names may appear here (tools/params_check.py).
SIM_WIND_SPD 0           # no wind
SIM_WIND_DIR 0
SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE 25.2    # 6S, full
SIM_BATT_CAP_AH 10
FRAME_CLASS 1            # quad
FRAME_TYPE 1             # X
MOT_THST_HOVER 0.45      # start value for the learned hover throttle (frame file's hoverThrOut)
MOT_SPIN_MAX 0.90
ATC_ANGLE_MAX 35         # degrees; above the default, so the ground's tilt warning comes early
# Rate gains: ArduPilot's defaults divided by how much more roll and pitch authority the
# 7-inch has than sd_quad14 per unit of motor output (thrust x arm / inertia: about 3.9x
# in roll, 2.8x in pitch); yaw a little lower than the default.
ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.035
ATC_RAT_RLL_I 0.035
ATC_RAT_RLL_D 0.0009
ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.05
ATC_RAT_PIT_I 0.05
ATC_RAT_PIT_D 0.0013
ATC_RAT_YAW_P 0.12
ATC_RAT_YAW_I 0.012
# Drag for the EKF's wind estimate and dead reckoning: SITL's own "Suggested EK3_DRAG_..."
# for this frame (test_drag_matches_sitl_suggestion keeps them within 10 %).
EK3_DRAG_BCOEF_X 39.417
EK3_DRAG_BCOEF_Y 39.417
EK3_DRAG_MCOEF 0.082
